               </text>
            </section>
            <section>
               <title value="Hospital course note"/>
               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear Colleague, I am writing to inform you regarding your patient, an 84-year-old male admitted on 16/01/2007 with an acute exacerbation of known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, the patient presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination confirmed bilateral decreased air entry with expiratory wheeze. Chest X-ray showed hyperinflation without consolidation. Arterial blood gas analysis revealed mild hypoxaemia with compensated respiratory acidosis. Blood tests showed elevated inflammatory markers. The patient was treated with nebulised bronchodilators, systemic corticosteroids, supplemental oxygen therapy, and supportive intravenous fluids. Vital signs were monitored closely throughout the stay. The patient responded well to treatment with significant symptomatic improvement. He was discharged on 17/01/2007 with an optimised inhaler regimen and oral steroid taper. Please arrange early follow-up and consider pulmonary rehabilitation referral. Yours sincerely.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
